Python ingestion writes to DuckDB; the browser app (Streamlit) reads only a versioned set of views, the data
contract.
{%- if motherduck %} `publish` copies the contract views to MotherDuck{% if cloud_run %}, where the hosted app on Cloud Run reads them{% endif %}.{% endif %}

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `uv run {{ project_name }} ingest <files>` | load data into `data/{{ db_file }}` |
| `uv run {{ project_name }} status` | what the database holds, and the contract check |
| `uv run {{ project_name }} app [--tailnet]` | the app at http://localhost:{{ app_port }} |
{%- if motherduck %}
| `uv run {{ project_name }} publish` | the contract views to MotherDuck (only when you ask) |
{%- endif %}
{%- if backup %}
| `uv run {{ project_name }} backup` | a verified Parquet snapshot in `backups/` |
{%- endif %}

